    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "key insight",
      "narration_text": "The straight line is not approximate. It follows from the Gamow factor — the WKB tunneling probability through the Coulomb barrier. A small change in decay energy changes the barrier width, which changes the tunneling probability exponentially. That exponential sensitivity is why 20 orders of magnitude map onto a straight log-scale line.",
