      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "governing equation",
      "narration_text": "Geiger-Nuttall law: log of lambda equals A minus B over root E-alpha. Lambda is the decay constant in inverse seconds. E-alpha is the decay energy in MeV. A and B are constants that depend on the atomic number. The law was empirical in 1911 — Gamow explained it with quantum mechanics in 1928.",
